  "Écris avec des quantificateurs ce que veut dire {l}.": "Write with quantifiers what {l} means.",
  "Quelle conclusion ?": "Which conclusion?",
  "Pour tout ε > 0, avec δ = {d} : si 0 < |{x}| ≤ δ, alors |{g}| ≤ ε. Donc la limite vaut {L}.": "For every ε > 0, with δ = {d}: if 0 < |{x}| ≤ δ, then |{g}| ≤ ε. So the limit is {L}.",
  "Il existe δ > 0 tel que pour tout ε > 0 : si 0 < |{x}| ≤ δ, alors |{g}| ≤ ε.": "There is a δ > 0 such that for every ε > 0: if 0 < |{x}| ≤ δ, then |{g}| ≤ ε.",
  "Pour ε = 0,01, δ = {d} convient : donc la limite vaut {L}.": "For ε = 0,01, δ = {d} works: so the limit is {L}.",
  "Pour tout x, il existe ε > 0 tel que |{g}| ≤ ε.": "For every x, there is an ε > 0 such that |{g}| ≤ ε.",
  "Pour tout ε > 0, δ = {d} convient.": "For every ε > 0, δ = {d} works.",
  "Écris l'écart {s} en fonction de |x − x₀|, puis choisis δ.": "Write the gap {s} in terms of |x − x₀|, then choose δ.",
  "Montre avec la définition que {l}.": "Show with the definition that {l}.",
  "Écart et δ": "Gap and δ",
  "Pour prouver lim<sub>x→3</sub> x² = 9, δ = ε/|x + 3| convient.": "To prove lim<sub>x→3</sub> x² = 9, δ = ε/|x + 3| works.",
  "Faux : δ est choisi avant x, il ne peut pas en dépendre. Avec |x − 3| ≤ 1, |x + 3| ≤ 7 : δ = min(1 ; ε/7).": "False: δ is chosen before x, it cannot depend on it. With |x − 3| ≤ 1, |x + 3| ≤ 7: δ = min(1 ; ε/7).",
  "Pour lim<sub>x→{x0}</sub> x² = {sq}, δ = ε/{M} convient pour tout ε > 0.": "For lim<sub>x→{x0}</sub> x² = {sq}, δ = ε/{M} works for every ε > 0.",
  "Faux : la borne |x + {x0}| ≤ {M} suppose |x − {x0}| ≤ 1. Pour ε = 20, δ = 20/{M} > 1 et x = {x0} + δ donne |x² − {sq}| = δ(δ + {x2}) > 20. Il faut δ = min(1 ; ε/{M}).": "False: the bound |x + {x0}| ≤ {M} assumes |x − {x0}| ≤ 1. For ε = 20, δ = 20/{M} > 1 and x = {x0} + δ gives |x² − {sq}| = δ(δ + {x2}) > 20. You need δ = min(1 ; ε/{M}).",
  "Pour lim<sub>x→1</sub> ({a}x {op} {b}) = {L}, δ = {a}ε convient pour tout ε > 0.": "For lim<sub>x→1</sub> ({a}x {op} {b}) = {L}, δ = {a}ε works for every ε > 0.",
  "Faux : |{g}| = {a}|x − 1| peut valoir {a}·{a}ε > ε. Il faut δ = ε/{a}.": "False: |{g}| = {a}|x − 1| can be {a}·{a}ε > ε. You need δ = ε/{a}.",
  "Pour lim<sub>x→2</sub> ({a}x − 1) = {L}, δ = ε/{a} convient pour tout ε > 0.": "For lim<sub>x→2</sub> ({a}x − 1) = {L}, δ = ε/{a} works for every ε > 0.",
  "Vrai : |f(x) − {L}| = {a}|x − 2| ≤ {a}·ε/{a} = ε.": "True: |f(x) − {L}| = {a}|x − 2| ≤ {a}·ε/{a} = ε.",
